[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593465338","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2593465338","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2593465338,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6alSP6","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-15T16:59:57Z","updated_at":"2025-01-15T16:59:57Z","body":"> The whitepoint also acts strangely with values lower than `1.0`. This issue doesn't occur in Forward+.\r\n\r\nValues lower than 1.0 will result in negative white parameters being passed to the shader. A value of exactly 1.0 will result in a value of 0.0 being passed to the shader. Seems I’ll need to do some digging into why this might sometimes be a problem with Compatibility.\r\n\r\nOriginally I had the `log2` calculation happening in the shader and I thought it worked fine for all ranges of white in Compatibility, so maybe the problematic behaviour is specific to passing the zero/negative values as a parameter to the shader.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593465338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593496157","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2593496157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2593496157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6alZxd","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-15T17:12:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-15T17:15:36Z","body":"> Tested locally, there's an issue in Compatibility if White is exactly `1.0`:\r\n\r\nStrange, I can't reproduce using the latest build artifact from this PR:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c649c94-1471-4be7-8c41-80178f87b655)\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.beta (a934213ba) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 980 Ti (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.4665) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 thread