 Would you be able to post a screenshot of this behaviour?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593986573/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596335242","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2596335242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2596335242,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6awO6K","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T17:41:00Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T17:41:00Z","body":"> Tested locally, there's an issue in Compatibility if White is exactly `1.0`:\r\n> ...\r\n> The whitepoint also acts strangely with values lower than `1.0`. This issue doesn't occur in Forward+.\r\n\r\nAh-ha! I have been able to reproduce this on my end. Thanks, @Calinou -- I'll dig into this issue and see if I can work around it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596335242/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596672864","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2596672864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2596672864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6axhVg","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T19:30:32Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T21:12:16Z","body":"> > Tested locally, there's an issue in Compatibility if White is exactly `1.0`:\r\n> > ...\r\n> > The whitepoint also acts strangely with values lower than `1.0`. This issue doesn't occur in Forward+.\r\n> \r\n> Ah-ha! I have been able to reproduce this on my end. Thanks, @Calinou -- I'll dig into this issue and see if I can work around it.\r\n\r\nOn my end, this issue appears to be a build-related issue that has nothing to do with this PR. Would you mind deleting all `.gen.h` files from `drivers\\gles3` and its subfolders and rebuilding, then let me know if that fixes the problem for you? Additionally, the build artifact from this PR should also work, as it doesn't suffer from this build issue....","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596672864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2597118074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2597118074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2597118074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6azOB6","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T23:30:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T23:31:08Z","body":"> On my end, this issue appears to be a build-related issue that has nothing to do with this PR. Would you mind deleting all `.gen.h` files from `drivers\\gles3` and its subfolders and rebuilding, then let me know if that fixes the problem for you? Additionally, the build artifact from this PR should also work, as it doesn't suffer from this build issue....\r\n\r\nI've done a clean build and can't reproduce the issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2597118074/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599328897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2599328897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2599328897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a7pyB","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T22:42:15Z","updated_at":"2025-01-19T03:44:27Z","body":"> I've done a clean build and can't reproduce the issue.\r\n\r\nThanks for the review!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this approach does have some downsides. The sigmoid contrast curve seems to be designed with a white value of ~16.29. A lower white value introduces not only higher contrast, but also a different relative scaling of channels, which means hue shift can pop up in some extreme cases like this one:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf7e4ed6-bce9-4377-ae69-9a00d568c852)\r\n\r\n(Note the lower `white` value produces a larger hue shift towards blue as the color approaches black.)\r\n\r\nIt's possible that the matrices were also designed with a specific white value in mind as well, but I don't yet understand that part of AgX, so I can't comment on it yet.\r\n\r\nFor this reason, I don't think this PR is a perfect \"silver bullet\" solution... Let me know if anyone has other ideas, but otherwise this might be the best way to deal with the limited dynamic range issue that the mobile renderer experiences.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599328897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2602945079","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2602945079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2602945079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bJco3","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-20T17:22:43Z","updated_at":"2025-01-20T17:22:43Z","body":"Rebased to include #101515.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2602945079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2607257878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2607257878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2607257878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bZ5kW","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-22T13:30:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-22T13:30:58Z","body":"I’m looking more into the sigmoid contrast curve right now and how it might adjust in relation to different max exposures. While I look into this, I’m marking this PR as a draft.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2607257878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2634806738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101559#issuecomment-2634806738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101559","id":2634806738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dC_XS","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-04T18:55:37Z","updated_at":"2025-02-04T18:55:37Z","body":"AgX is designed to have a middle grey value of `0.18`. This means that the film-like contrast curve uses a linear input value of `0.18` as its inflection point: a `0.18` input will always result in `0.18` output, regardless of the white/min/max exposure settings of the tonemapper. [This piece of code](https://github.com/EaryChow/AgX_LUT_Gen/blob/ab7415eca3cbeb14fd55deb1de6d7b2d699a1bb9/AgXBaseRec2020.py#L36-L39) is the critical line that ensures that the `x_pivot` (inflection point of the curve) is always at a value of middle grey (0.18). This same line [exists in Troy's original AgX configuration](https://github.com/sobotka/SB2383-Configuration-Generation/blob/74bff1547505e751d6f0605ca65834b6c7e99a8f/generate_config.py#L60C1-L67C6).\r\n\r\nThe `0.18` middle grey was likely chosen because this is an ACES standard that is used in a lot of HDR processing. Here are some links that help demonstrate the `0.18` middle grey value in AgX was not an arbitrary choice:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/imageworks/OpenColorIO-Configs/blob/master/aces_1.0.3/python/aces_ocio/colorspaces/aces.py (0.18 used as a middle grey)\r\nhttps://community.acescentral.com/t/is-mid-gray-nit-setting-in-st2084-based-on-0-18-in-scene-linear-not-18-mid-gray/3531\r\nhttps://community.acescentral.com/t/ue5-ssta-input-unit/5245\r\nhttps://github.com/colour-science/aces-dev/blob/86284e2f145a89e3612f05ec7ea5a3e9d92cc779/documents/LaTeX/S-2014-003/appendixC.tex#L28\r\n\r\nThis PR incorrectly adjusts the middle grey value as the white parameter is changed, which results in lower white values becoming very bright:\r\n\r\n| 16.0 white | 2.0 white\r\n| --- | ---\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1240404c-d586-4910-9d54-63f2e8c73959) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8a7037c-4d01-4e10-9ed6-45c7dc05c495)\r\n\r\nClosing as superseded by #102425, which correctly implements white parameter support.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2634806738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]